# LOOT CRATES REGISTRY. Read at build time by bolt: ctf_loot:config puts it into the storage
# ctf_loot:config (rarities, tasks, task settings). Full description: MECHANICS.md
#
# During a round (and end_round) an attacker can complete tasks by chance. At the start of the
# next freeze a shulker box with a reward falls for him (for the rarest task he completed),
# onto a landing point of the map (ctf_maps:map/<map>/loot). Only he can open it.

# RARITIES, from the most common one: rank = number in the list (1..5).
#   name - sign text; box - the shulker box; from_color -> color - the falling trail (RGB 0..1);
#   text_color; reward - the test item of the rarity (for "give"; for now wool blocks)
RARITIES = [
    {
        "id": "common",
        "name": "COMMON",
        "box": "light_gray_shulker_box",
        "from_color": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25],
